From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CEB-GNRD board layer <bmc@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] peci: retry response-in-progress completion code

Physical GNR-D hardware returns completion code 0x83 during package
configuration reads. The pinned kernel treats it as unknown and returns
EIO, causing intermittent CPU discovery and temperature read failures.

Follow the upstream GNR support proposal and map response-in-progress to
EAGAIN. Reuse the existing retry bit, exponential backoff and 700 ms retry
window. Persistent failures still return ETIMEDOUT; no stale temperature
is substituted and no failed request is treated as successful.

Reference: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260928075956.62298-4-changhuang.liang@starfivetech.com/
Upstream-Status: Pending [adapted from upstream PECI GNR support proposal]
---
 drivers/peci/request.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/peci/request.c b/drivers/peci/request.c
--- a/drivers/peci/request.c
+++ b/drivers/peci/request.c
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@
 #define PECI_CC_NEED_RETRY			0x80
 #define PECI_CC_OUT_OF_RESOURCE			0x81
 #define PECI_CC_UNAVAIL_RESOURCE		0x82
+#define PECI_CC_RESP_IN_PROGRESS		0x83
 #define PECI_CC_INVALID_REQ			0x90
 #define PECI_CC_MCA_ERROR			0x91
 #define PECI_CC_CATASTROPHIC_MCA_ERROR		0x93
@@ -112,6 +113,7 @@ int peci_request_status(struct peci_request *req)
 	case PECI_CC_NEED_RETRY:
 	case PECI_CC_OUT_OF_RESOURCE:
 	case PECI_CC_UNAVAIL_RESOURCE:
+	case PECI_CC_RESP_IN_PROGRESS:
 		return -EAGAIN;
 	case PECI_CC_INVALID_REQ:
 		return -EINVAL;
